(>> 5.3 Encapsulation and Access Modifiers) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Python enforces encapsulation through naming conventions rather than strict access) Tj
T*
(keywords \(public/private\):) Tj
T*
(* Public Attributes: Standard identifiers accessible everywhere \(self.name\).) Tj
T*
(* Protected Attributes: Prefixed with a single underscore \(_self._name\). Indicates) Tj
T*
(internal use; accessible by subclasses.) Tj
T*
(* Private Attributes & Name Mangling: Prefixed with double underscores) Tj
T*
(\(__self.__secret\). CPython automatically mangles the name to _ClassName__secret to) Tj
T*
(prevent accidental override by subclasses.) Tj
T*
(* Property Decorators \(@property, @attr.setter\): Implement pythonic getters and) Tj
T*
(setters with validation logic without changing public access syntax.) Tj
T*
