(\(mangles\) the name by prefixing it with an underscore followed by the class name:) Tj
T*
(_ClassName__attribute. This prevents accidental namespace collisions and unintended) Tj
T*
(overriding by subclasses. It is NOT strict security: code can still access or mutate the) Tj
T*
(mangled name via obj._ClassName__balance.) Tj
T*
(* Q2: Explain the C3 Linearization Algorithm and Method Resolution Order \(MRO\) in) Tj
T*
(multiple inheritance.) Tj
T*
(Answer: When a class inherits from multiple parents, Python resolves method lookups) Tj
T*
(along a deterministic sequence called the Method Resolution Order \(MRO\). Python uses the) Tj
T*
(C3 Linearization Algorithm to compute MRO, ensuring three properties: \(1\) Children) Tj
T*
(precede parents. \(2\) Multiple parent listing order is preserved. \(3\) Monotonicity: if) Tj
T*
(class A precedes B in one class MRO, it must precede B in all derived MROs. The sequence) Tj
T*
(can be inspected via Class.mro\(\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
